  "body": "Red on mote at 5fce31b40 (origin/main b712adb84 + the ggbdpq port batch, none of which touches the code under test), `go test -tags nogui -count=3 ./internal/provider/`, one of three runs:\n\n```\n--- FAIL: TestCodexSubagentModelsKept (0.03s)\n    codex_subagent_kept_test.go:37: asking Codex's subagent models again allocated 557056 bytes, building them 1797528\n```\n\nLikely cause: `allocatedBy` reads `runtime.MemStats.TotalAlloc` before and after, which counts every goroutine in the test binary. Background work an earlier test left running (refresh loops, the log lines around it show Codex/Claude switching from other tests at the same second) allocates during the kept measurement, so `kept*4 > built` can trip without the cache being missed. Not reproduced by injection yet.\n\nA fix measures what the call itself does: `testing.AllocsPerRun`, or a count of how often the catalog is copied, instead of process-wide bytes.\n\nAn earlier single run of the package on the same tree also ended FAIL; its log was cut by tail, so which test is not known.",
  "closed_by": null,
