     "body": "`go test ./internal/provider -count=1 -timeout 45m` went red once at d84d2d4d7 (the gateway memory series rebased onto 1bd99194e; nothing under internal/provider changed), darwin arm64, go1.26.8, under load from other sessions' suites:\n\n```\n--- FAIL: TestClaudeAccountServesModelsListedSinceItsFetch (0.00s)\n    claude_models_test.go:52: claude: {ID: Name: ... Account:<nil>} false\n```\n\n`find(All(), \"claude\")` found no Claude row right after `claudeSignIn`. The test passes alone (`-count=5`) and with `-run Claude` (24s), so it depends on the order of the whole package. Candidates: 1bd99194e (Claude Code listed signed out) or c087834d6 (rememberLogins' time check before logins.json's lock), with state left over from an earlier test.\n\nNot taken yet; whoever picks it up, say so here first.\n",
