   "body": "A test-only fix is on [the fork branch](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/5435-subagent-kept-fewest), commit [50e61864b](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/50e61864b0dd85cf3ffbcacb551999d8bd7121ff), based on ed0ab567.\n\nThe measurement now uses `leastBytes`, the package's existing five-round fewest check, instead of averaging process-wide `TotalAlloc` over ten runs. Taking the least of five rounds reduces interference from occasional background allocations while retaining the same `kept*4 > built` bound. It still reads process-wide bytes: sustained background activity can affect every round, so this is a mitigation, not a proof of attribution to one call. `allocatedBy` stays for its other callers.\n\n`TestCodexSubagentModelsKept` passes `-count=3` under `-race`, and provider vet, the full offline nogui build, formatting and diff checks pass. The full package run is red on `TestPluginCheckinAsksAgainAtUntil` and `TestSignInDoneOnceTheAccountIsBack` from a race inside plugin `Cached`'s background refresh; with this change stashed they fail the same on the pristine base, so they are unrelated to this branch. AI-assisted implementation and review.",
